            <div xml:id="d714">

                <pb facs="1003" n="993" sameAs="frus:frus1945v07/pg993"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/2–2045: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Atcheson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Chungking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-02-20T17:00:00+07:00">February 20,
                            1945—5 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received February 20—2:45 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>261. On February 16, General Hurley made informal oral approach to T. V. Soong in
                    regard to the possibility of amnesty for political <pb facs="1004" n="994"
                        xml:id="pg994"/> prisoners in Sinkiang (ReDeptel 181, February 2); the
                    following day Soong informed General Hurley that he had referred matter to
                    Generalissimo.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Atcheson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
